infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title Renaming via template literals multiplies key sets
  desc Each key axis you cross-multiply in an as clause explodes the union — remapping amplifies the blow-up
  order asc
  sequences
    - label 1 key set — 50-member union
      desc One template over a 50-key source builds 50 string literals. Snappy editor, instant hovers.
    - label 2 key sets — 2,500-member union
      desc Cross-product of two 50-key sets in a single as clause: 50 x 50 = 2,500 literals built in one step.
    - label 3 key sets — 125,000 members, past the cap
      desc 50 x 50 x 50 = 125,000 blows past TypeScript's ~100,000-member union cap: type too complex to represent, multi-second hovers.
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
